  "nativeProtocol": [
    "Send official update-ref --no-deref --stdin: start, planned expected-OID operation and prepare. Keep stdin open after prepare: ok.",
    "Observe the ref with official symbolic-ref --quiet --no-recurse while the prepared native lock is held.",
    "Commit the direct-ref case; abort the observed alias case. A competing official writer receives128 and does not alter the prepared lock.",
    "EOF without commit causes native abort/release in the observed case. A pre-existing lock is refused and preserved."
  ],
  "conclusions": [
    "A native prepared lock permits a read-only direct/symbolic type observation before authorizing commit, closing the demonstrated ordinary Git writer race for this prototype.",
    "No-deref alone is insufficient: NO-DEREF-PROBE.json shows that expected-OID update can replace an alias. The prepared type guard separately refuses alias adoption.",
    "The dangling zero-expected case is refused during native prepare, without replacing the dangling alias. Its128 is the expected conservative observation, not a successful update.",
    "The native EOF and abort behavior released only locks owned by those observed native processes; the prototype did not delete disputed locks.",
    "Node orchestrates the official Git transaction protocol; this does not create a parallel object store, version history, ref storage or versioning protocol."
  ],
